\subsection{Federated clustering simulation}

To probe deployment under data siloing we use federated $k$-means, with centroid aggregation in the manner of federated averaging (FedAvg) \cite{fedavg2017}. We do not propose a new federated method. The 2\,542 records are assigned by patient to ten simulated sites. In the independent and identically distributed (IID) setting each patient is assigned to a site at random. In the non-IID setting the patients of each class are split across the sites by proportions drawn from a Dirichlet distribution with concentration 0.3. The sites then differ sharply in arrhythmia prevalence. Sites with fewer than two records are dropped. In each of 15 rounds every site runs three local Lloyd iterations from the shared centroids. The server then averages the site centroids, weighted by their cluster counts. Each of ten seeds draws a new partition and a new initialisation. Two steps use the pooled records: the power transform is fitted on all records, and the initial centroids are drawn from all records. The heterogeneity is therefore a simulated class-proportion skew across ten partitions of one dataset. We report the ARI of the final global centroids beside centralized $k$-means with ten initialisations on the same conditioned representation.

\section{Results}\label{sec:results}

\subsection{Clustering by representation and algorithm}

Table~\ref{tab:main} and Fig.~\ref{fig:heatmap} summarise the PTB-XL benchmark. ECGFounder clusters best (ARI up to 0.885 with $k$-means), and the hand-crafted features reach 0.711 with Ward. HuBERT-ECG reaches at most 0.195. Raw flattening and the conv-AE score at chance (ARI at most 0.013). Across the four clusterers given the number of classes, the ARI of the hand-crafted features ranges from 0.544 to 0.711 and that of ECGFounder from 0.709 to 0.885. Across representations, the $k$-means ARI ranges from 0.000 to 0.885. In this setting, the choice of representation changed the result more than the choice of clusterer.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{PTB-XL SR-versus-AF on 2\,542 recordings (1\,282 SR, 1\,260 AF): clustering ARI by representation and clusterer under power scaling, and the supervised ceiling. Each $k$-means, spectral and GMM entry is the mean over ten seeds that vary only the initialisation. Each Ward and HDBSCAN entry is one deterministic fit. The seed standard deviation of the $k$-means ARI is 0.000 for raw flattening, the hand-crafted features and HuBERT-ECG, and 0.001 for ECGFounder. The 95\% half-width over seeds is 0.008 for raw flattening with the GMM and below 0.001 for the other seeded entries of raw flattening and the hand-crafted features. The ceiling is the patient-grouped five-fold accuracy of a balanced logistic regression, against a majority-class baseline of 0.504. The random-labelling ARI is 0.000. Paired Wilcoxon tests compare the representations adjacent in the $k$-means ranking of ECGFounder, the hand-crafted features, HuBERT-ECG and raw flattening. The three contrasts reach $p = 0.002$, the floor for ten paired seeds, with effect sizes, the differences in mean ARI, of 0.242, 0.470 and 0.174. The conv-AE was not tested. The dimension of each representation is given in parentheses.}
